Here is the structured goal model for the multi-robot food delivery and dish retrieval system:

### Goal Model Table

| **Goal ID** | **Goal Title** | **Goal Text** | **Runtime Annotation** | **Goal Type** | **Target Condition/Enquired Information** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|-------------|----------------|---------------|------------------------|---------------|--------------------------------------------|---------------|--------------------|
| **G1**      | Overall Mission | Deliver food and retrieve dishes | Sequential (;) | Achieve | Food delivered and dishes retrieved | - | Mission objective |
| **G2**      | Food Delivery   | Deliver meals to patients | AND | Achieve | Meals delivered correctly | G1; | Both delivery and retrieval are essential |
| **G2.1**    | Direct Delivery | Robot places food directly | - | Perform | Food placed on table | AND | Direct method is a sub-goal |
| **AT1**     | Direct Delivery Task | Robot delivers to room | - | Task | Execute at inpatient room | G2.1 | Single robot action |
| **G2.2**    | Tray Retrieval  | Inpatient retrieves from tray | AND | Achieve | Food retrieved correctly | G2; | Tray retrieval is necessary |
| **G2.2.1**  | Check Ability   | Determine if inpatient can retrieve | Sequential (;) | Query | Inpatient ability status | G2.2 | Need info for decision |
| **G2.2.2**  | Inpatient Retrieval | Inpatient fetches food | - | Perform | Food retrieved | G2.2; | If able, proceed |
| **G2.2.3**  | Assistance Needed | Get help for retrieval | OR | Achieve | Assistance provided | G2.2 | Either robot or human can help |
| **AT2**     | Robot Assistance | Robot helps retrieve | - | Task | Execute at room | G2.2.3 | Single robot assistance |
| **AT3**     | Human Assistance | Human helps retrieve | - | Task | Execute at room | G2.2.3 | Human intervention needed |
| **G2.3**    | Correct Meal Retrieval | Ensure correct meal | - | Achieve | Correct meal retrieved | G2 | Track and verify meals |
| **G3**      | Dish Retrieval  | Collect dirty dishes | AND | Achieve | Dishes collected | G1; | Essential for hygiene |
| **G3.1**    | Unassisted Retrieval | Robot collects dishes | - | Perform | Dishes collected | G3 | Robot can handle alone |
| **G3.2**    | Robot Assistance | Two robots collect | - | Perform | Dishes collected | G3 | Teamwork for heavy loads |
| **G3.3**    | Human Retrieval | Human collects dishes | - | Perform | Dishes collected | G3 | Human help when needed |

### Task Model Table

| **Task ID** | **Task Title** | **Task Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|-------------|----------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|-----------------------|--------------------|
| **AT1**     | Direct Delivery | Robot delivers food | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Single robot action |
| **AT2**     | Robot Assistance | Assists retrieval | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Single robot help |
| **AT3**     | Human Assistance | Assists retrieval | AND | Inpatient room | 0 | Human intervention |
| **G2.2.2**  | Inpatient Retrieval | Fetches food | AND | Inpatient room | 0 | Inpatient action |
| **G3.1**    | Unassisted Retrieval | Collects dishes | AND | Inpatient room | 1 | Single robot task |
| **G3.2**    | Robot Assistance | Two robots collect | AND | Inpatient room | 2 | Teamwork for efficiency |
| **G3.3**    | Human Retrieval | Collects dishes | AND | Inpatient room | 0 | Human assistance |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both food delivery and dish retrieval are essential for the mission.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2, G2.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: All methods of food delivery must be considered.

- **G2.2 -> G2.2.1, G2.2.2, G2.2.3 [OR]**  
  Justification: Determining ability leads to either inpatient or assistance.

- **G2.2.3 -> AT2, AT3 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either robot or human can assist.

This model ensures all aspects of the mission are covered, with clear hierarchical decomposition and justifications.
